:answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476187}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3c6ffd8f-aed0-5462-a678-623c3eb10c91" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(6p-6)x=36x\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=6p-6,\\,b=36.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\n6p-6=36.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6p & =42 \\\\ p & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476183 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c43f225d-c7fc-52aa-b515-2cae7955625c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476190}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476190} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8023800-07d9-51cc-a72e-06d399d2f3a0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8af6ded4-48a3-5261-b74f-acd5512ac6e3" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(5p-3)x=37x\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=5p-3,\\,b=37.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\n5p-3=37.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5p & =40 \\\\ p & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476185 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b22cba07-0bc4-5800-81fe-2be13fe3a58b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476186}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476186} :answer-field/id #uuid "81d03035-2a65-5a2d-8446-1f0fcb459162" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a0e66191-a3c9-5572-8227-0f5cb2926471" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(3p-1)x=17x\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=3p-1,\\,b=17.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\n3p-1=17.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p & =18 \\\\ p & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476189 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce549a5e-11a0-5494-87aa-29777e280cf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476192}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476192} :answer-field/id #uuid "127f3283-4330-5bc1-ae69-19de1c8c9f76" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476178}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c2e51c73-6455-54ee-866f-56127d07e55b" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(7p-1)x=20x\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=7p-1,\\,b=20.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\n7p-1=20.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7p & =21 \\\\ p & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476193 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a63ee0f-09e0-5d67-bf7b-6c6205d50d30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476180} {:answer/id #uuid "83fd7c44-dbb6-5a68-92eb-ccaed9e31428" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476182} {:answer/id #uuid "9014217b-66f1-54ef-a298-df27f02ad1bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476184} {:answer/id #uuid "c5a26fc8-6112-50b6-a54e-0893e7fb061f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476191} {:answer/id #uuid "f215b6e0-2e13-5777-a13e-ee5f86401b00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476196}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476196} :answer-field/id #uuid "eccd13b2-ec61-50c2-8c46-2af59c18fcd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476195}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e320282a-d753-5114-aed7-fb576099a4d8" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n7px=2x\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $p?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=7p,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\n7p=2.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\np=\\frac{2}{7}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491998 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "651c6521-6052-5754-9de3-5d4d268af61b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491636}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491636} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d5121d0-bbcc-54ac-a60e-be4b2f5b9f0d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491902}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1b724bdb-17d7-5012-9f30-50cac17a9c4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-288570" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(-t-2)x=x\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is a constant. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $t?$\n\n$t=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=-t-2,\\,b=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\n-t-2=1.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-t & =3 \\\\ t & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549009 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bc56c0e-abb3-5e53-818e-6aa51cc4af57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548439} {:answer/id #uuid "36c25fee-f58b-5409-a5a6-477628433eda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548463} {:answer/id #uuid "5ade53e2-0afe-522f-a54b-d5db209e2043" :answer/type {:db/iden