3034} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b7c28ee-4474-52da-a1df-71e406689457" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "021c858c-ff29-5406-946e-12cf5966af05" :question/math-academy-id "q-288441" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n7mx=-14x\n$$\n\nwhere $m$ is a constant. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $m?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=7m,\\,b=-14.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\n7m=-14.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $m,$ we get\n\n$$\nm=-2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555761 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b03681d2-3f8d-5d5a-b665-08eb5334df77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555422}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555422} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8685c5a-c976-5c4d-ba32-65fdf5654aca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "06a0435e-893d-5476-8004-8e6faf0aa039" :question/math-academy-id "q-288569" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(4r-6)x=22x\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $r?$\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=4r-6,\\,b=22.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\n4r-6=22.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4r & =28 \\\\ r & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110721 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110371 :question/id #uuid "6eeec12a-5da8-5113-916a-58f4ca807207" :question/math-academy-id "e-18852" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(k+4)x + 3r = 6x + 12\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ and $r$ are constants. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $k+r?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax + b = cx + d\n$$\n\nwhere $a, b, c,$ and $d$ are constants. This equation has infinitely many solutions if \n\n$$\na = c\\quad \\text{and}\\quad b = d.\n$$\n\nTo determine the values of $k$ and $r$ such that the equation\n\n$$\n(k+4)x + 3r = 6x + 12\n$$\n\nhas infinitely many solutions, we equate the coefficients of $x,$ and we equate the constants:\n\n- Equating the coefficients of $x,$ we have\n\n$$\nk + 4 = 6.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equating the constants, we have\n\n$$\n3r = 12.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $k = 2$ and $r = 4,$ we have\n\n$$\nk + r = 2+4 = 6.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b1fd794-f42b-5316-80e9-0698cb1f8b87" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186477026 :question-generator/id #uuid "a8a3fd9e-9b0f-54b0-b19c-26e749314cab" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186110721.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111136 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2918787-6369-5281-b839-56303be60818" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186108557} {:answer/id #uuid "d22c7204-b52f-5b6a-ad06-733bfdf